  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Creating Dignified Lives for 1.000+ Asylum Seekers</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Habibi.Works is a free-to-use, community-organized maker space bringing together asylum-seekers, international makers, and Greek locals to share knowledge, skills, and experiences. Situated just 300 meters across from the Katsikas refugee camp, the 15 different working areas, ranging from wood and metal work to IT classes and music production, center the needs of individuals, working at eye level with them to create a space where individual freedom, potential, and agency can be restored.</narrative>
  </description>
